    "created_at": "2020-03-27T14:30:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-03-27T14:30:57Z",
    "body": "I *thought* we may want another destination when I wasn't sure if these SVGs can run script, but looks like they can't. So, I'm fine with aligning them as an \"image\" destination and aligning Chromium's implementation to deal with that when it comes to preload. (I'm not sure if `ResourceType::kSVGDocument` is something we can get rid of, but that would be the cleanest...)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
