    "created_at": "2024-09-11T13:51:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-11T13:54:39Z",
    "body": "> Another point to consider: the SVG document, when loaded using a `<use>` tag, doesn't seem to be able to run script, so maybe an \"image\" destination is the right call (and the Chromium implementation would have to somehow deal with that SVG documents are images too).\r\n> \r\n> /cc @yutakahirano @mikewest\r\n\r\nWhile neither use, nor image will run script within <script> tags.\r\n\r\n- use will run javascript event handlers but image will not.\r\n- use can load external references e.g. other use elements but image cannot load any external references.\r\n- use must be same domain as the loading content but image need not be.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
